Subject: ssl: guard the local iovec redefinition on wasi

bio_ssl.cc intentionally redefines `struct iovec` locally to avoid
having to include <sys/socket.h> via bio.h on consumers. On wasi
targets wasi-libc's __struct_iovec.h is already pulled in through the
headers openssl/ssl.h transitively includes, so the local definition
becomes a genuine redefinition error.

Skip the local definition when __wasi__ is set — the system
definition's layout (void *iov_base, size_t iov_len) is identical to
the one AWS-LC declares here.

--- a/ssl/bio_ssl.cc
+++ b/ssl/bio_ssl.cc
@@ -14,10 +14,14 @@
 // implement such checks, making this approach necessary for compatibility.
 //
 // See commit aws-lc@9db959e for more details.
+#if defined(__wasi__)
+// wasi-libc already provides struct iovec via <__struct_iovec.h>.
+#else
 struct iovec {
   void* iov_base;
   size_t iov_len;
 };
+#endif

 static SSL *get_ssl(BIO *bio) {
   return reinterpret_cast<SSL *>(bio->ptr);
